<title>GERMANY: SCHERING H1 GP NET PROFIT UP AT 294 MLN DMK.</title>
<headline>SCHERING H1 GP NET PROFIT UP AT 294 MLN DMK.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to the end of June 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   294     vs 244</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   477     vs 351</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     498     vs 416</p>
<p>    Post-tax profit			    294     vs 244</p>
<p>    Group sales				  3,103   vs 2,566</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>     Domestic				    503     vs 375</p>
<p>     Foreign				     2,600   vs 2,191</p>
<p>    Group payroll				21,175  up 11 percent</p>
<p>    Payroll costs				973     vs 839</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German pharmaceuticals group is Schering AG. The group said its AgrEvo joint-venture contributed 46 million marks to earnings, compared to 60 million in the same period last year. The group said that first half sales of its Betaferon product rose 24 percent to 327 million marks. Schering said it saw 1997 profit rising by up to 20 percent.</p>
</text>
